{% comment %}
  RAQI Redesign — §2.2 Header.

  ⚠ The four nav items are HARD-CODED ON PURPOSE. Shopify navigation menus are
  store-level linklists shared with the live theme "Raqi box" (188008038707);
  reading or editing one here would change the live storefront. At go-live the
  linklist is switched over manually as a separate, deliberate step.

  "Discovery Set" resolves to the in-page anchor on the homepage panel, never to
  /pages/discovery-box — that page is unpublished and returns 404 by design.

  2026-08-29: WhatsApp added to the utility row (icon only, monochrome, inherits
  the row's link colour like the other utility links). Hidden below the rd-hide-sm
  breakpoint — on mobile the floating button in snippets/raqi-whatsapp-float.liquid
  covers it. Number is also in that snippet, sections/footer-group.json and
  templates/page.contact.json — keep the four in sync.

  2026-08-30: that snippet was named here but had never actually been created on
  this theme, so between the rd-hide-sm breakpoint and the bottom of the page
  there was no WhatsApp entry point on mobile at all. It exists now and is
  rendered below. The float shows at <=900px and this icon at 901px and up —
  the same breakpoint from both sides. Move one and you must move the other.

  2026-09-03: the burger button existed and was styled, but nothing listened to
  it — this section carried no JavaScript at all, and raqi-redesign.css had no
  open state for .rd-nav, only `display:none` below 900px. So the mobile menu
  was never built rather than broken. Added the panel, its styles and its
  script here, self-contained, so the shared stylesheet stays untouched.

  The panel also carries Search, WhatsApp and عربي, which are .rd-hide-sm and
  therefore invisible below 900px — without them the mobile menu would offer
  less than the desktop header does.

  Stacking: WhatsApp float 500 < this panel 800 < cart drawer 900, so opening
  the cart covers the menu rather than fighting it.

  2026-09-03b: visual pass on that panel. It worked but had never been given the
  redesign's own treatment — a bare &times; glyph floated above the links, 4px
  between nav rows, no panel header, no rule work, and the shared stylesheet
  still has no .rd-menu rules at all (grep raqi-redesign.css for "rd-menu": zero
  hits), so it was rendering on Minimog leftovers rather than on the system.
  Rebuilt against the §1 tokens and the §2.5 ruled-table motif already used by
  "How a decant is made" and the cart drawer:

    · panel header — RAQI/راقي wordmark left, hairline circular ✕ right, on its
      own rule. The close control now has a 40px tap target and an axis to sit
      on instead of hanging off the top-right corner.
    · nav — Italiana 30px on a ruled list, 20px of block padding per row. No
      index numerals: Shop/Brands/Discovery Set/Our Story are destinations,
      not steps, and this system already reserves numbering for the things
      that genuinely are ordered (.rd-steps__num on "How a decant is made",
      .rd-bld__step-n on the builder). The only marked row is the current
      page, via aria-current.
    · utilities — pushed to the foot behind an "Elsewhere" eyebrow, with عربي
      promoted out of the link run into a bordered chip so the language switch
      reads as a control rather than a fifth link.
    · motion — scrim fade + panel slide on the cart drawer's own curve
      (cubic-bezier(.22,.61,.36,1)), contents rising on a short stagger, and a
      real close animation: close() now holds the panel for 200ms behind an
      .is-closing class before setting [hidden], so dismissing no longer snaps.
      The timeout always fires, so [hidden] is set even if the animation is
      dropped. prefers-reduced-motion takes the instant path on both.

  Colours are the six §1 tokens only, type is Italiana/Karla via --rd-display /
  --rd-body, so the panel inherits the Arabic faces automatically under
  html[lang="ar"] like the rest of the redesign.

  2026-09-03c: the عربي switch never worked, in the header or the panel. Both
  links were href set to routes.root_url — the root of the locale you are
  ALREADY in — so tapping عربي reloaded the English homepage. Verified against
  the Admin API: `ar` IS a published, non-primary locale on this store, and the
  UAE market (subfolderSuffix "ae") serves it from /ar-ae/, so there was a real
  destination to point at the whole time. Rebuilt as a genuine toggle — see the
  liquid block below — that preserves the current page and the query string.

  2026-09-03d: the chrome is now translatable. Every literal English string in
  this section moved to a `| t` key under raqi.rd.* (English in
  locales/en.default.json). Previously this section carried zero translation
  keys, so the nav stayed English on /ar-ae/ no matter what.
{% endcomment %}
{% render 'rd-fonts' %}

{%- liquid
  assign shop_url = routes.all_products_collection_url
  assign brands_url = routes.collections_url
  # pages['about'].url is locale-aware (Shopify prefixes *.url with the
  # current locale root), unlike routes.root_url | append: 'pages/about',
  # which produced '/ar-aepages/about' — a 404 — on the Arabic storefront.
  assign story_url = pages['about'].url | default: '/pages/about'
  assign here = request.path

  # --- Language switch target -------------------------------------------
  # Both عربي links used to point at routes.root_url. That is the root of the
  # locale you are ALREADY in, so the link reloaded the homepage in the same
  # language — it never switched anything. Arabic is a published locale on
  # this store (ar, non-primary) served from the UAE market's /ar-ae
  # subfolder, so the target has to be built from the other language's own
  # root_url.
  #
  # Strip the current locale's root prefix off request.path and re-attach the
  # target language's, so the visitor lands on the SAME page translated
  # rather than being dropped on the homepage. The query string is carried
  # over too, so ?preview_theme_id= survives the switch while this theme is
  # still a draft. Same approach as snippets/raqi-language-switcher.liquid,
  # which already got this right; this section never called it.
  assign en_lang = null
  assign ar_lang = null
  for lang in localization.available_languages
    if lang.iso_code == 'en'
      assign en_lang = lang
    elsif lang.iso_code == 'ar'
      assign ar_lang = lang
    endif
  endfor

  assign is_ar = false
  if request.locale.iso_code == 'ar'
    assign is_ar = true
  endif

  assign target_lang = ar_lang
  assign target_label = 'عربي'
  assign target_code = 'ar'
  if is_ar
    assign target_lang = en_lang
    assign target_label = 'English'
    assign target_code = 'en'
  endif

  # The '/' guard matters: this market uses /en-ae and /ar-ae so root_url is
  # never bare, but on a market without a subfolder it would be '/', and
  # remove_first would then eat the leading slash and yield '/ar-aeproducts/x'.
  assign locale_root = localization.language.root_url
  assign path_suffix = request.path
  if locale_root != blank and locale_root != '/' and path_suffix contains locale_root
    assign path_suffix = path_suffix | remove_first: locale_root
  endif

  assign lang_href = ''
  if target_lang
    assign lang_href = target_lang.root_url | append: path_suffix
    if request.query_string != blank
      assign lang_href = lang_href | append: '?' | append: request.query_string
    endif
  endif
-%}

<div class="rd-scope">
  <header class="rd-header">
    <div class="rd-header__inner">
      <button class="rd-header__burger" type="button" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="rd-menu" data-rd-burger>
        <span></span><span></span><span></span>
      </button>

      <nav class="rd-nav" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">{{ 'raqi.rd.nav.shop' | t }}</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.collections_url }}">{{ 'raqi.rd.nav.brands' | t }}</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}#discovery-set">{{ 'raqi.rd.nav.discovery_set' | t }}</a>
        <a href="{{ story_url }}">{{ 'raqi.rd.nav.our_story' | t }}</a>
      </nav>

      <a class="rd-logo" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" aria-label="{{ shop.name }} — home">
        <span class="rd-logo__en">RAQI</span>
        <span class="rd-logo__ar" lang="ar">راقي</span>
      </a>

      <div class="rd-header__right">
        <a class="rd-hide-sm" href="{{ routes.search_url }}">{{ 'raqi.rd.utils.search' | t }}</a>
        <a class="rd-header__wa rd-hide-sm" href="https://wa.me/971585670055" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Chat with RAQI on WhatsApp" title="{{ 'raqi.rd.utils.whatsapp' | t }}">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M17.472 14.382c-.297-.149-1.758-.867-2.03-.967-.273-.099-.471-.148-.67.15-.197.297-.767.966-.94 1.164-.173.199-.347.223-.644.075-.297-.15-1.255-.463-2.39-1.475-.883-.788-1.48-1.761-1.653-2.059-.173-.297-.018-.458.13-.606.134-.133.298-.347.446-.52.149-.174.198-.298.298-.497.099-.198.05-.371-.025-.52-.075-.149-.669-1.612-.916-2.207-.242-.579-.487-.5-.669-.51-.173-.008-.371-.01-.57-.01-.198 0-.52.074-.792.372-.272.297-1.04 1.016-1.04 2.479 0 1.462 1.065 2.875 1.213 3.074.149.198 2.096 3.2 5.077 4.487.709.306 1.262.489 1.694.625.712.227 1.36.195 1.872.118.571-.085 1.758-.719 2.006-1.413.248-.694.248-1.289.173-1.413-.074-.124-.272-.198-.57-.347m-5.421 7.403h-.004a9.87 9.87 0 0 1-5.031-1.378l-.361-.214-3.741.982.998-3.648-.235-.374a9.86 9.86 0 0 1-1.51-5.26c.001-5.45 4.436-9.884 9.888-9.884 2.64 0 5.122 1.03 6.988 2.898a9.825 9.825 0 0 1 2.893 6.994c-.003 5.45-4.437 9.885-9.885 9.885m8.413-18.297A11.815 11.815 0 0 0 12.05 0C5.495 0 .16 5.335.157 11.892c0 2.096.547 4.142 1.588 5.945L.057 24l6.305-1.654a11.882 11.882 0 0 0 5.683 1.448h.005c6.554 0 11.89-5.335 11.893-11.893A11.821 11.821 0 0 0 20.464 3.488"/></svg>
        </a>
        {%- if target_lang -%}
          <a class="rd-header__lang rd-hide-sm" href="{{ lang_href }}" hreflang="{{ target_code }}" lang="{{ target_code }}">{{ target_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
        <a class="rd-header__bag" href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" data-rd-bag>{{ 'raqi.rd.utils.bag' | t }} (<span data-rd-bagcount>{{ cart.item_count }}</span>)</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="rd-menu" id="rd-menu" data-rd-menu hidden>
    <div class="rd-menu__scrim" data-rd-menu-close></div>
    <div class="rd-menu__panel" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Menu">

      <div class="rd-menu__head">
        <span class="rd-menu__mark" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="rd-menu__mark-en">RAQI</span>
          <span class="rd-menu__mark-ar" lang="ar">راقي</span>
        </span>
        <button class="rd-menu__close" type="button" aria-label="Close menu" data-rd-menu-close>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <path d="M3 3 L13 13 M13 3 L3 13" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>

      <nav class="rd-menu__nav" aria-label="Primary mobile">
        <a href="{{ shop_url }}"{% if here == shop_url %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ 'raqi.rd.nav.shop' | t }}</a>
        <a href="{{ brands_url }}"{% if here == brands_url %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ 'raqi.rd.nav.brands' | t }}</a>
        <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}#discovery-set">{{ 'raqi.rd.nav.discovery_set' | t }}</a>
        <a href="{{ story_url }}"{% if here == story_url %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ 'raqi.rd.nav.our_story' | t }}</a>
      </nav>

      <div class="rd-menu__utils">
        <span class="rd-menu__eyebrow">{{ 'raqi.rd.utils.elsewhere' | t }}</span>
        <div class="rd-menu__links">
          <a href="{{ routes.search_url }}">{{ 'raqi.rd.utils.search' | t }}</a>
          <a href="https://wa.me/971585670055" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{ 'raqi.rd.utils.whatsapp' | t }}</a>
        </div>
        {%- if target_lang -%}
          <a href="{{ lang_href }}" hreflang="{{ target_code }}" lang="{{ target_code }}" class="rd-menu__lang">{{ target_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% render 'raqi-whatsapp-float' %}
</div>

{% style %}
  .rd-header__wa {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    line-height: 0;
  }

  .rd-header__wa svg {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    display: block;
  }

  /* The switcher now names the language you'd switch TO, so on the Arabic
     storefront it reads "English" and must drop the Arabic face. Beats the
     unconditional !important on .rd-header__lang in raqi-redesign.css. */
  .rd-header__lang[lang="en"] {
    font-family: var(--rd-body) !important;
    text-transform: uppercase !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em !important;
  }

  /* Mobile menu. Hidden outright above the burger's breakpoint so a stale open
     state can never leak onto desktop. */
  .rd-menu[hidden] { display: none; }
  .rd-menu { display: none; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .rd-menu { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 800; display: block; }

    .rd-menu__scrim {
      position: absolute; inset: 0;
      background: rgba(34, 38, 31, 0.45);
      animation: rd-menu-fade 220ms ease both;
    }

    .rd-menu__panel {
      position: absolute; inset-block: 0; inset-inline-start: 0;
      inline-size: min(86vw, 360px);
      background: var(--rd-bone);
      border-inline-end: 1px solid var(--rd-rule);
      padding: 24px 24px calc(28px + env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px));
      display: flex; flex-direction: column;
      overflow-y: auto;
      transform: translateX(0);
      animation: rd-menu-in 260ms cubic-bezier(.22, .61, .36, 1) both;
    }

    [dir="rtl"] .rd-menu__panel { animation-name: rd-menu-in-rtl; }

    @keyframes rd-menu-fade     { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }
    @keyframes rd-menu-in       { from { transform: translateX(-100%); } to { transform: translateX(0); } }
    @keyframes rd-menu-in-rtl   { from { transform: translateX(100%);  } to { transform: translateX(0); } }
    @keyframes rd-menu-rise     { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(9px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }

    /* Contents rise on a short stagger behind the panel edge. */
    .rd-menu__head,
    .rd-menu__nav a,
    .rd-menu__utils { animation: rd-menu-rise 420ms cubic-bezier(.22, .61, .36, 1) both; }
    .rd-menu__head          { animation-delay: 90ms; }
    .rd-menu__nav a:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: 130ms; }
    .rd-menu__nav a:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 170ms; }
    .rd-menu__nav a:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 210ms; }
    .rd-menu__nav a:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 250ms; }
    .rd-menu__utils         { animation-delay: 290ms; }

    /* Dismissal. The panel is held for 200ms by the script behind .is-closing
       so it slides out instead of snapping; the staggered children are frozen
       flat first or their fill would hold them mid-rise. */
    .rd-menu.is-closing .rd-menu__head,
    .rd-menu.is-closing .rd-menu__nav a,
    .rd-menu.is-closing .rd-menu__utils { animation: none; }
    .rd-menu.is-closing .rd-menu__scrim { animation: rd-menu-fade 200ms ease both reverse; }
    .rd-menu.is-closing .rd-menu__panel { animation: rd-menu-in 200ms ease both reverse; }
    [dir="rtl"] .rd-menu.is-closing .rd-menu__panel { animation-name: rd-menu-in-rtl; }

    /* Panel header — wordmark on the left, close on the right, one rule under. */
    .rd-menu__head {
      display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 16px; padding-block-end: 20px;
      border-block-end: 1px solid var(--rd-rule);
    }
    .rd-menu__mark { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 9px; line-height: 1; }
    .rd-menu__mark-en {
      font-family: var(--rd-display); font-size: 21px;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--rd-wine);
    }
    .rd-menu__mark-ar {
      font-family: var(--rd-display-ar); font-size: 13px;
      color: var(--rd-wine); opacity: 0.75;
    }
    .rd-menu__close {
      flex: 0 0 auto; inline-size: 40px; block-size: 40px;
      margin-inline-end: -6px;
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      background: none; border: 1px solid var(--rd-rule); border-radius: 50%;
      color: var(--rd-grey); cursor: pointer; padding: 0;
      transition: color 200ms ease, border-color 200ms ease;
    }
    .rd-menu__close svg { inline-size: 14px; block-size: 14px; display: block; }
    .rd-menu__close:active { color: var(--rd-wine); border-color: var(--rd-wine); }

    /* Nav — Italiana on a ruled list. No index numerals: the four destinations
       are not a sequence, and this system reserves numbering for things that
       genuinely are (.rd-steps__num, .rd-bld__step-n). Rank comes from the
       rules and the block rhythm; the only marked row is the current page. */
    .rd-menu__nav { display: flex; flex-direction: column; margin-block-start: 6px; }
    .rd-menu__nav a {
      display: block; padding-block: 20px;
      border-block-end: 1px solid var(--rd-rule);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-family: var(--rd-display); font-weight: 400;
      font-size: 30px; line-height: 1.12; color: var(--rd-ink);
      transition: color 200ms ease;
    }
    .rd-menu__nav a:last-child { border-block-end: 0; }
    .rd-menu__nav a:active,
    .rd-menu__nav a[aria-current="page"] { color: var(--rd-wine); }

    /* Utilities — held at the foot, behind their own eyebrow and rule. */
    .rd-menu__utils {
      margin-block-start: auto; padding-block-start: 26px;
      border-block-start: 1px solid var(--rd-rule);
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px;
    }
    .rd-menu__eyebrow {
      font-family: var(--rd-body); font-size: 10px;
      letter-spacing: 0.24em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--rd-wine);
    }
    .rd-menu__links { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
    .rd-menu__utils a {
      font-family: var(--rd-body); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--rd-grey); text-decoration: none;
    }
    .rd-menu__utils a:active { color: var(--rd-ink); }
    /* Scoped past `.rd-menu__utils a` on specificity rather than !important,
       so the chip can restate the Arabic face and drop the uppercase run. */
    .rd-menu__utils a.rd-menu__lang {
      font-family: var(--rd-body-ar);
      text-transform: none; letter-spacing: 0;
      font-size: 14px; color: var(--rd-wine);
      border: 1px solid var(--rd-rule); padding: 9px 18px;
      margin-block-start: 4px;
    }
    .rd-menu__utils a.rd-menu__lang:active { border-color: var(--rd-wine); }
    /* Same flip as the desktop chip when the target language is English. */
    .rd-menu__utils a.rd-menu__lang[lang="en"] {
      font-family: var(--rd-body);
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.18em; font-size: 12px;
    }
  }

  /* Scroll lock while the panel is open. */
  html.rd-menu-open, html.rd-menu-open body { overflow: hidden; }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .rd-menu__panel,
    .rd-menu__scrim,
    .rd-menu__head,
    .rd-menu__nav a,
    .rd-menu__utils,
    .rd-menu.is-closing .rd-menu__panel,
    .rd-menu.is-closing .rd-menu__scrim { animation: none; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<script>
(function () {
  var burger = document.querySelector('[data-rd-burger]');
  var menu   = document.querySelector('[data-rd-menu]');
  if (!burger || !menu) return;

  // Must match the .is-closing animation duration above.
  var CLOSE_MS = 200;

  var lastFocus  = null;
  var closeTimer = null;

  function reducedMotion() {
    return !!(window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches);
  }

  // Always reached: close() schedules this on a timeout rather than waiting on
  // animationend, so a dropped or interrupted animation still sets [hidden].
  function finishClose() {
    closeTimer = null;
    menu.hidden = true;
    menu.classList.remove('is-closing');
    document.documentElement.classList.remove('rd-menu-open');
    if (lastFocus && lastFocus.focus) lastFocus.focus();
  }

  function open() {
    if (closeTimer) { clearTimeout(closeTimer); closeTimer = null; }
    menu.classList.remove('is-closing');
    menu.hidden = false;
    burger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
    document.documentElement.classList.add('rd-menu-open');
    lastFocus = document.activeElement;
    var closeBtn = menu.querySelector('.rd-menu__close');
    if (closeBtn) closeBtn.focus();
  }

  function close() {
    if (menu.hidden || closeTimer) return;
    burger.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
    if (reducedMotion()) { finishClose(); return; }
    menu.classList.add('is-closing');
    closeTimer = setTimeout(finishClose, CLOSE_MS);
  }

  // Mid-dismissal counts as closed, so tapping the burger again re-opens
  // rather than toggling back into another close.
  function isOpen() { return !menu.hidden && !closeTimer; }

  burger.addEventListener('click', function () { isOpen() ? close() : open(); });

  menu.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    if (e.target.closest('[data-rd-menu-close]')) close();
  });

  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
    if (e.key === 'Escape' && isOpen()) close();
  });

  // A link inside the panel navigates; the in-page #discovery-set anchor does
  // not, so close on any link tap or the panel would stay over the target.
  menu.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    if (e.target.closest('a')) close();
  });

  // Resizing past the burger's breakpoint leaves an open panel unreachable and
  // the scroll lock stuck, so drop it.
  if (window.matchMedia) {
    var mq = window.matchMedia('(min-width: 901px)');
    var onChange = function (ev) { if (ev.matches && isOpen()) close(); };
    if (mq.addEventListener) mq.addEventListener('change', onChange);
    else if (mq.addListener) mq.addListener(onChange);
  }
})();
</script>

<script>
(function () {
  // 2026-09-05: the header's Bag link carried a data-rd-bag hook, but nothing
  // ever listened to it — the script above handles only the burger menu — so
  // the browser just followed href="/cart" and left the page. The drawer it
  // should have opened is already mounted on every page via header-group.
  //
  // The anchor keeps its real href, so with JS off it still reaches /cart. With
  // JS on, the click is intercepted and raises the SAME event Add to Bag
  // raises; sections/rd-cart-drawer.liquid already listens for it and already
  // falls back to navigating when its own markup is missing, so the fallback
  // is inherited rather than duplicated here.
  document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    var bag = (e.target && e.target.closest) ? e.target.closest('[data-rd-bag]') : null;
    if (!bag) return;
    // Modified and non-primary clicks keep native behaviour, so open-in-new-tab
    // and middle-click still work on what is still a real link.
    if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.shiftKey || e.altKey || e.button) return;
    // No drawer on this page at all: leave the href alone rather than dead-end.
    if (!document.getElementById('rd-cart-drawer')) return;
    try {
      e.preventDefault();
      document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('cart:refresh', { detail: { open: true } }));
    } catch (err) {
      window.location.href = bag.getAttribute('href');   // never swallow the tap
    }
  });
})();
</script>

